        "original_id": "10b3ae05-63b4-534e-8f51-d6dc3f4eb8eb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Liliʻuokalani\n- Places: Hawaii, Kingdom of Hawaii\n- Works: \"Aloha ʻOe\"\n- Concepts: Hawaiian cultural symbols\n\nFacts:\n- Liliʻuokalani was born as Lydia Liliʻu Loloku Walania Wewehi Kamakaʻeha on September 2, 1838.\n- Liliʻuokalani was the last monarch of the Kingdom of Hawaii.\n- Liliʻuokalani ruled the Kingdom of Hawaii from January 29, 1891 until the overthrow of the Kingdom of Hawaii on January 17, 1893.\n- \"Aloha ʻOe\" is Liliʻuokalani's most famous song.\n- \"Aloha ʻOe\" is a common cultural symbol for Hawaii.\n- Liliʻuokalani died on November 11, 1917.",
